```c
spin_lock(&vnode->lock);
afs_lock_may_be_available(vnode);
```
Reason:
The `__afs_break_callback()` function acquires `vnode->lock` before calling `afs_lock_may_be_available()`, which also attempts to acquire the same lock. This results in a double locking scenario, potentially leading to deadlocks.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
// spin_lock(&vnode->lock); // This line is removed
if (vnode->lock_state == AFS_VNODE_LOCK_WAITING_FOR_CB)
```
